Subject: [PATCH] A beam of light casts no shadow of itself

Patch 0056 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-12: "beams themselves now cast shadows of their own so they cause shadows
inside themselves ... beams of "light" must never be castiing a shadow of the beams themselves".
The foliage rule (0017) makes a see-through draw of more than two triangles that reads depth a
solid traced surface, and 0039 takes back out only the draws its shaft test passes. A beam that
fails that test stayed solid: in every shadow ray's way, blocking the windows' light and the
beam lights along it, and shaded like a wall before the composite.

Four candidate rules for which see-through draws are light, each its own Debugging switch in
tuneLightTest.z (bits 1 a fading texture, 2 a gray texture, 4 an added blend, 8 a long shape).
A draw any switched rule passes becomes what 0039 makes a shaft: a see-through overlay no ray
traces, drawn after the composite in its own brightness. The lights 0029 and 0030 make are
untouched. beamFromDraw's point gathering and axes are taken out as drawPoints and drawAxes so
the long shape test reads the same points.

